-- title:
--   Characters annihilating r on congruent unit idèles
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois and $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K) = (L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L)$ commutative, let $\psi$ be a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to $\mathbb{C}^{\times}$, let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, let $\mathfrak{m}'$ be an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_K$ not divisible by $v$, and let $N$ be a natural number. Assume `hN`: for every non-zero $\beta \in \mathcal{O}_K$ and every ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ such that the principal fractional ideal $(\beta)$ has valuation-count $0$ at all primes dividing $\mathfrak{m}$, if $\tau(\beta) > 0$ for every real embedding $\tau$ of $K$ and $\beta - 1 \in v^{N}\mathfrak{m}'$, then $\psi$ of the ray Artin symbol `artinSymbol K L 𝔪` of $(\beta)$ — the multiplicative extension to ideals coprime to $\mathfrak{m}$ of $w \mapsto$ `artinFrob K L w`, the arithmetic Frobenius at the chosen prime of $L$ above $w$ — equals $1$. Let $\mathfrak{f}$ be an ideal which is admissible of degree $[L:K]$: $\mathfrak{f} \neq \bot$, and $w^{e}\mid\mathfrak{f}$ with $e =$ `admissibleExpOfDegree K (Module.finrank K L) w` for every finite place $w$ of $K$ at which the inertia subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ of the chosen prime above $w$ is non-trivial. Let $r\colon (\mathbb{A}_K)^{\times} \to \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be a homomorphism on the idèle units such that: the principal idèles (the image of $K^{\times}$) lie in $\ker r$; $\ker r$ is the subgroup generated by the principal idèles together with the image of the idelic norm of `genuineBaseChange K L` from $(\mathbb{A}_L)^{\times}$; $r$ is surjective; and for every idèle $u$ with `IsAdjuster K 𝔣 u 1`, that is, with finite component of valuation $1$ and with $u_w - 1$ of valuation at most $\exp(-\mathrm{ord}_w \mathfrak{f})$ at each $w \mid \mathfrak{f}$, and with $\mathrm{archRealProjTau}$ positive at every real embedding, one has $r(u) = \prod_{w}^{\mathrm{f}} \,$`artinFrob K L w`$^{\,\mathrm{ord}_w(u)}$, the finitely-supported product over the finite places, where $\mathrm{ord}_w(u) = -\log$ of the valuation of the $w$-component of the finite part of $u$. Then for every idèle unit $x$ satisfying `IsAdjuster K (v.asIdeal ^ N * 𝔪') x 1`, with trivial infinite part $\mathrm{infPart}\,x = 1$ and with all finite components of valuation $1$, one has $\psi(r(x)) = 1$.
--
--   This is the bridge from the ray-class (Artin symbol) formulation of the reciprocity condition on $\psi$ to its idelic formulation: an abelian character killing the Artin symbols of totally positive generators congruent to $1$ modulo $v^{N}\mathfrak{m}'$ kills $\psi \circ r$ on all unit idèles satisfying the corresponding congruence, including those supported at places outside $v\mathfrak{m}'$. It is used in the determination of the local conductor exponent, by [`ArtinL.Abelian.apply_artinSymbol_eq_one_of_sub_one_mem_pow_mul_of_conductorExponent_le_u0`](thm.html#ArtinL.Abelian.apply_artinSymbol_eq_one_of_sub_one_mem_pow_mul_of_conductorExponent_le_u0) and [`ArtinL.Abelian.exists_apply_artinSymbol_ne_one_of_one_le_conductorExponent_u0`](thm.html#ArtinL.Abelian.exists_apply_artinSymbol_ne_one_of_one_le_conductorExponent_u0).
